# openHC — BCM53125 managed switch (DSA/b53) kernel side. Shared by EA variants
# that HAVE the switch: ea3-v1, ea3-v2, ea1-v2-poe.
#
# Three pieces: (1) the SPI master spi-pxa2xx-pci on PCI 8086:2e6a; (2) the b53
# switch driver; (3) board glue spi-ea-b53-board.c, which registers the switch at
# CS 1 and hands DSA the port map (CPU=5, jacks=1 and 2) as platform_data since
# there is no DTB. DSA's bring-up of port 1 is still UNVERIFIED (the stock config
# isolates it); if DSA does not attach, S40net falls back to the master and only
# the primary jack works, so the board stays reachable either way.
#
# COMMON_CLK is NOT optional: SPI_PXA2XX_PCI is a derived symbol
# (def_tristate SPI_PXA2XX && PCI && COMMON_CLK), so setting CONFIG_SPI_PXA2XX_PCI
# directly is silently DROPPED. Without COMMON_CLK the SPI master never binds
# 8086:2e6a, the board_info never instantiates, and b53 never probes (measured:
# 01:0b.4 with no driver, empty /sys/class/spi_master). Do not "clean up" below.
CONFIG_COMMON_CLK=y
CONFIG_SPI=y
CONFIG_SPI_MASTER=y
CONFIG_SPI_PXA2XX=y
#
# The b53 symbols are CONFIG_B53 / CONFIG_B53_SPI_DRIVER — NOT CONFIG_NET_DSA_B53*,
# which this fragment said for a long time: those names do not exist, kconfig
# dropped them silently, and b53 was never built (spi92.1 appeared with modalias
# spi:bcm53125 but /sys/bus/spi/drivers/ was empty). B53 selects the BRCM tags.
#
# MODULES, not built-in: an x86_64 EA-3 bzImage is right at CEFDK's 7,417,856-byte
# window and DSA + b53 + tag codecs are the slice that pushes it over; as modules
# they load from p1 after mount. SAFE because the glue (spi-ea-b53-board.c, obj-y,
# subsys_initcall) only registers the SPI board_info and calls NO b53/dsa symbol,
# so there is no obj-y→module link dependency; the module binds the already-
# registered device by deferred probe. S39ea-switch modprobes b53_spi BEFORE
# S40net so DSA still attaches at boot. The SPI master stays =y (the bus the
# device sits on).
#
# BRIDGE + VLAN_8021Q are =m too: the bigger Buildroot 2026.02 toolchain compiles
# the 7.1.8 kernel ~100 KB larger and the switch boards (ea3-v1, ea1-v2-poe) ran
# over CEFDK's 7,417,856-byte bzImage window; CONFIG_BRIDGE built in is ~60 KB.
# They are on-demand network features, so they move to p1 — S39ea-switch modprobes
# them (DSA wants bridging present; loading before S40net keeps that true).
CONFIG_NET_DSA=m
CONFIG_B53=m
CONFIG_B53_SPI_DRIVER=m
CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_BRCM=m
CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_BRCM_PREPEND=m
CONFIG_BRIDGE=m
CONFIG_VLAN_8021Q=m
